# Full test suite only

## Default gate (one run)

When validating a change or finishing a task, run the **complete** suite **once**:

```
./vendor/bin/sail artisan test --parallel --coverage --min=90
```

## Separate check (also once)

Code coverage and type coverage are **different** checks. Do **not** merge them into one command. After the gate above passes, run type coverage **once** if finishing the task:

```
./vendor/bin/sail artisan test --type-coverage --min=90 --parallel
```

## Do not

- Finish with only one file, folder, or `--filter`
- Re-run the same suite with a lower `--min` (e.g. 0) — if `--min=90` passes, lower would too; if it fails, you already know
- Run the full suite multiple times “just to be sure” with different thresholds
- Treat a green subset as “tests passed”

## Exception

A single file/filter is allowed **only** while diagnosing a failure. After the fix, run the **default gate once** before considering the work done.

Also run the linter when finishing:

```
./vendor/bin/sail exec laravel.test vendor/bin/pint --parallel
```
